Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
=================================

The circuit geometry in this directory, with the one exception noted below, is a
Derived Database produced from OpenStreetMap data. It is NOT covered by the MIT
licence in the repository root.

    (c) OpenStreetMap contributors
    Source:  https://www.openstreetmap.org/
    Licence: Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
             https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

ODbL is share-alike. If you publicly use these files, or any database derived
from them, you must offer that database under ODbL and keep this attribution.
Software that merely reads these files is not itself covered: ODbL applies to the
database, not to programs that process it.

Elevation samples come from SRTM, served by OpenTopoData. SRTM is public domain
and carries no further obligation.


Exception
---------

testcircuit.json is an original fictional layout, authored from waypoints in
Tools/build_track.py. It contains no OpenStreetMap data and no elevation samples,
so it is covered by the MIT licence in the repository root like the rest of the
project. Each file states its own provenance in its "attribution" field.


On circuit names
----------------

These files reproduce layout geometry only, which is factual. Circuit names,
logos, sponsor artwork and liveries are not reproduced and are not licensed here.
Every catalogue entry carries an in-game alias instead, so the Spa-Francorchamps
layout ships as "Ardennes Circuit".
